{
  "id": "chapman-oxygen-photochemistry-third-science",
  "name": "Closed oxygen Chapman photochemistry with conserved oxygen atoms",
  "description": "Photolysis, three-body stabilization with a fixed inert bath, and O+O3 destruction retain atom stoichiometry. The oxygen-only mechanism omits catalytic HOx/NOx/halogen cycles, transport and radiation transfer and cannot predict actual ozone abundance. Illustrative normalized concentrations O0,O2one,O3zero and effective rates0.001,0.1,1,0.05. Constant third-body concentration is absorbed into recombination; constant illumination. Horizon800,RK4step0.1. These are not atmospheric rate constants or a chosen stratospheric altitude. Original mathematical transcription/adaptation; not a calibrated forecast. Signed net-rate flows implement the stated equations. No numerical clamps or hidden resets.",
  "category": "physics",
  "source": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19810008106/downloads/19810008106.pdf",
  "reference": "Malkin (1978), Environmental Impact Statement for the Space Shuttle Program, NASA-TM-82278, AppendixD Chapman four-reaction oxygen photochemistry; NTRS19810008106.",
